+
+The existing trusted finite guardian owns this object. Arbitrary jobs must be
+separate protected PID/mount namespaces; never pass this object, either socket,
+or its bootstrap key to a job. PR_SET_DUMPABLE alone is not that separation.
+No provider credential appears on the job protocol. The pinned native executor
+receives bounded bytes and an opaque job scope only. Runtime admission remains
+closed until the complete native graph and namespace/credential split are proved.
